<%# BMI hero result — regenerated from spec issue #53 against DESIGN.md (BLEND).

    A richer-than-a-single-number answer (DESIGN.md §4 "Hero-result"): the big
    tabular-nums BMI on a surface card with the 5px coral left rule, the WHO category as a
    green accent badge (positive-stat green, DESIGN.md §1), and a thin stacked bar
    (DESIGN.md §4 "Charts — thin stacked bar") plotting the four broad WHO bins across a
    15–40 window with a marker pinning this person's BMI and the band containing them
    lifted to accent green. A text legend carries the bands so meaning never rests on
    colour alone (DESIGN.md §6).

    `calc:` is a valid Calculators::Bmi; the rendered result keys are `bmi` + `category`
    (the JSON envelope's result shape, ARCHITECTURE.md §4). %>
<% bmi = calc.result[:bmi] %>
<% category = calc.result[:category] %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
    <%# The 5px coral left rule (DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result). %>
    <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Body Mass Index</p>
      <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
        <p class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= bmi_display(bmi) %></p>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-faint">kg/m&sup2;</p>
      </div>

      <%# Category badge — the WHO band as a green accent chip. The text is the meaning;
          colour is reinforcement, not the sole signal (DESIGN.md §6). %>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-bold text-accent">
          <%= category %>
        </span>
      </p>

      <%# WHO classification scale — a thin stacked bar over the 15–40 window. Each broad
          bin sizes to its share of the window; the active bin (the one containing this
          BMI) lifts to accent green, and a marker tick pins the exact BMI. The bar is
          decorative — the legend below names the bands as text. %>
      <div class="mt-6">
        <div class="relative">
          <div class="flex h-2.5 overflow-hidden rounded-full" role="presentation">
            <% bmi_scale_bands(bmi).each do |band| %>
              <span class="block h-full <%= band[:active] ? "bg-accent" : "bg-rule" %>"
                    style="width: <%= band[:width] %>%" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <%# Marker — a thin ink tick at this BMI's position along the bar. It lives in the
              relative wrapper (not the overflow-hidden bar) so it is never clipped. %>
          <span class="absolute -top-1 h-4.5 w-0.5 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-ink"
                style="left: <%= bmi_marker_position(bmi) %>%" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </div>

        <%# Band legend — label + range, the active band in ink (with an accent dot), the
            rest faint. Carries the classification as text (DESIGN.md §6). %>
        <dl class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-xs sm:grid-cols-4">
          <% bmi_scale_bands(bmi).each do |band| %>
            <div class="<%= band[:active] ? "text-ink" : "text-faint" %>">
              <dt class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-bold">
                <% if band[:active] %><span class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><% end %>
                <%= band[:label] %>
              </dt>
              <dd class="mt-0.5 tabular-nums"><%= band[:range] %></dd>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
